ements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,¬(P\\text{ is not a rhombus}\\text{ and }Q\\text{ is not a rectangle}) & ≡¬((P\\text{ is not a rhombus})∧(Q\\text{ is not a rectangle})) \\\\  & ≡¬(P\\text{ is not a rhombus})∨¬(Q\\text{ is not a rectangle}) \\\\  & ≡(P\\text{ is a rhombus})∨(Q\\text{ is a rectangle}) \\\\  & ≡P\\text{ is a rhombus}\\text{ or }Q\\text{ is a rectangle}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9de08e2-7bf6-5ab5-bb90-7f2896dda1dc" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Sentence Containing a Conjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32492387-ba7d-5d00-8da5-c3fafa28d652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ is not positive or $0$ is not negative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376263} {:answer/id #uuid "1cd15e29-c32b-527d-8a98-6191e37915c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ is positive and $0$ is not negative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376264} {:answer/id #uuid "51cae14e-4a2e-54b5-845b-00b5deb85a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ is positive and $0$ is negative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376265} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd1346f-51cc-5c3e-a6e2-40bf2db7645f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ is positive or $0$ is not negative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376266} {:answer/id #uuid "26ef6c48-bac3-5888-8fc0-59a2d90bd66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ is positive or $0$ is negative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ef6c48-bac3-5888-8fc0-59a2d90bd66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ is positive or $0$ is negative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376267} :answer-field/id #uuid "50e54abe-1f17-5c28-b368-9fe5216a089b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376262}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "631284c1-8510-54b7-a4ad-a5b7e737bce8" :question/math-academy-id "q-182449" :question/problem "$\\,$ $0$ is not positive and $0$ is not negative.\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law posits that the negation of a conjunction of two statements is equivalent to the disjunction of the negated individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows.\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,¬(0\\text{ is not positive}\\text{ and }0\\text{ is not negative}) & ≡¬((0\\text{ is not positive})∧(0\\text{ is not negative})) \\\\  & ≡¬(0\\text{ is not positive})∨¬(0\\text{ is not negative}) \\\\  & ≡(0\\text{ is positive})∨(0\\text{ is negative}) \\\\  & ≡0\\text{ is positive}\\text{ or }0\\text{ is negative}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5bd766-d624-54e3-945e-7ae37b83886a" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Sentence Containing a Disjunction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a915252-8a28-59c6-bd86-2c6bd84206e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is not integer or $5$ is positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376376} {:answer/id #uuid "b5811ef9-2b42-5894-9f21-7047a2013a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is integer and $5$ is positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376377} {:answer/id #uuid "8a89247a-0549-585b-92c5-4e6b3d9ce6ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is not integer and $5$ is not positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376378} {:answer/id #uuid "38569278-a785-5845-b784-b36363593133" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is not integer or $5$ is not positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376379} {:answer/id #uuid "62267499-5148-5d1e-804d-cb2c7a19ad5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is not integer and $5$ is positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a89247a-0549-585b-92c5-4e6b3d9ce6ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ is not integer and $5$ is not positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376378} :answer-field/id #uuid "b28191e6-a805-5f54-8c92-ed941568714f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f6bb99a-3d7f-5bf0-9077-86786b3b9774" :question/math-academy-id "q-182617" :question/problem "$\\,$ $5$ is integer or $5$ is positive.\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?" :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that the negation of a disjunction of two statements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(5\\text{ is integer}\\text{ or }5\\text{ is positive}) & ≡¬((5\\text{ is integer})∨(5\\text{ is positive})) \\\\  & ≡¬(5\\text{ is integer})∧¬(5\\text{ is positive}) \\\\  & ≡(5\\text{ is not integer})∧(5\\text{ is not positive}) \\\\  & ≡5\\text{ is not integer}\\text{ and }5\\text{ is not positive}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9c85b7b-1326-5f25-aa21-ab115680582d" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Statement Using De Morgan's Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20acedc5-b294-5413-b17b-a5f3caa5c550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∨Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412386} {:answer/id #uuid "35e52632-f5b5-5772-ab79-32017923e196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬X∧Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412389} {:answer/id #uuid "7a601caa-cc1b-50ae-a2cc-5b34ed42a556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∨¬Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412393} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dba7c8-efea-5a6e-af84-29fb680cb947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬X∨Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412394} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e4a767-3062-5279-bea4-3a33192ca589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∧Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20acedc5-b294-5413-b17b-a5f3caa5c550" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "X∨Y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412386} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d7e4ae-4469-5ebc-b1c2-b83f60deb2be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ad44d3b-4c29-563d-b808-2a30dfb14db0" :question/math-academy-id "q-81866" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(¬X∧¬Y)$ using De Morgan's laws." :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(X∧Y)≡¬X∨¬Y, \\\\ ¬(X∨Y)≡¬X∧¬Y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(¬X∧¬Y) & ≡¬(¬X)∨¬(¬Y) \\\\  & ≡X∨Y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9c85b7b-1326-5f25-aa21-ab115680582d" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Statement Using De Morgan's Laws"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7f4b028-b351-53bb-a1e0-06459c553bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377860} {:answer/id #uuid "603c8fdd-37ce-5127-ac0b-80645793c34a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬A∨¬B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377861} {:answer/id #uuid "72b3357b-ff7a-5d9a-a739-9efa4115f5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∧¬B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377862} {:answer/id #uuid "90b8d944-0ee6-53eb-9ec4-cd0719a94924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "¬A∧B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377863} {:answer/id #uuid "91413da9-af6d-5cec-92c3-b7b16c278284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨¬B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91413da9-af6d-5cec-92c3-b7b16c278284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A∨¬B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377864} :answer-field/id #uuid "24466484-bded-5290-9119-b3c194d2d88d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e09e71d-719e-5316-87f5-f69ed972d79d" :question/math-academy-id "q-82019" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(¬A∧B)$ using De Morgan's laws." :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's laws state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(A∧B)≡¬A∨¬B, \\\\ ¬(A∨B)≡¬A∧¬B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can simplify the given statement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(¬A∧B) & ≡¬(¬A)∨¬(B) \\\\  & ≡A∨¬B\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
